WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.151
You can't manage what you can't see,

2
00:00:02.151 --> 00:00:05.263
and a CA's database only
shows what that CA issued.

3
00:00:05.263 --> 00:00:09.376
So the platform finds certificates
two ways: it scans the network for

4
00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:14.138
anything presenting a certificate, and
it imports what your CAs already issued.

5
00:00:14.138 --> 00:00:17.062
Agents and API feeds fill in the rest.

6
00:00:17.062 --> 00:00:18.919
The program's rule is blunt:

7
00:00:18.919 --> 00:00:23.224
any certificate found with no
record and no owner is a finding.

8
00:00:23.224 --> 00:00:28.700
In the first wave, run read-only scans
and imports, and log every surprise.
